omment":"4-501.114: The sanitizer concentration in the sanitizer bottle was recorded at less than 100ppm QUAT. PIC corrected this by increasing the concentration of the sanitizer to 200ppm QUAT. Ensure that test strips are utilized in the facility when creating the sanitizer to ensure its efficacy. \n4-501.114: Chemical sanitizer for manual or mechanical operation shall meet proper criteria: (A) chlorine shall have minimum temperature (55F), concentration (100ppm), and pH (10). (B) Iodine shall have 68F, pH of 5 or less and concentration of 12.5ppm and 25ppm. (C) Quaternary ammonium shall have 75F, concentration based on label, and water with 500ppm hardness or less. (D) - (E) Meets EPA-label use and regulatory authority approval. (P) (F) Other chemical sanitzers in-use shall have EPA-registered label, display device registration number on devide and is operated and maintained in accordance with manufacturers instructions (Pf)","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"497009","date":"2024-04-08","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=9085&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=497009&INSPECTION_NN=497009","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"474155","date":"2023-09-18","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":1,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=9085&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=474155&INSPECTION_NN=474155","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":55,"title":"Physical facilities installed, maintained, and clean","repeat":false,"comment":"6-101.11: The shelving in the dry storage room are observed to have bare wood where the food is stored. This was pointed out to the PIC and a solution of a coat of paint on the bare wood. Ensure all bare wood is sealed to create a smooth, nonabsorbent, and easily cleanable surface.\n6-101.11: (A) Materials indoor shall be SMOOTH, durable, and EASILY CLEANABLE. Areas subject to moisture must be Nonabsorbent. (B) In TEMPORARY FOOD ESTABLISHMENT, floor may be material effectively treated to control dust and mud. Walls and ceilings may be material that protects interior from weather and windblown dust and debris.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"447314","date":"2023-02-22","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":1,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=9085&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=447314&INSPECTION_NN=447314","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":55,"title":"Physical facilities installed, maintained, and clean","repeat":false,"comment":"6-501.11: The coving in the bathroom is observed to hav fallen off behind the toilet. Ensure this coving is reattached to the wall to create a smooth, nonabsorbent, and easily cleanable surface.\n6-501.11: PHYSICAL FACILITIES shall be maintained in good repair.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"433567","date":"2022-10-06","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=9085&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=433567&INSPECTION_NN=433567","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"411202","date":"2022-03-07","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=9085&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=411202&INSPECTION_NN=411202","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"401413","date":"2021-11-05","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail